Description: Build the tests with panic=unwind, so that cargo builds libstdbuf once.
 The release profile sets panic = "abort", but a test harness needs unwinding, so cargo test builds the dependencies of
 the test binaries with panic=unwind and those of the coreutils binary, which the tests run, with panic=abort.
 uu_stdbuf_libstdbuf is a dependency of both, and as a cdylib its file name has no hash, so both variants are linked to
 target/release/deps/libstdbuf.so, which cargo warns about as an "output filename collision". With thin LTO, which
 Tweak-release-build-profile.patch sets, both also write their intermediate objects into target/release/deps, named
 after the output, so the two links read and rewrite the same objects, one fails with "file truncated", and no test
 runs, as in 2 of 2 builds with 16 and 24 jobs. The test step now sets CARGO_PROFILE_RELEASE_PANIC=unwind, so that only
 one variant exists. The install step builds the binaries it installs afterwards with the release profile, as before.
Author: Mitar
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-13
--- a/debian/rules
+++ b/debian/rules
@@ -122,7 +122,7 @@
 	@echo "Skipping the test suite on s390x to stay under the buildd timeout"
 else
 	# for now, don't fail the build if tests are failing
-	CARGO_HOME=$(CURDIR)/debian/cargo_home make PROFILE=release MULTICALL=$(MULTICALL) \
+	CARGO_PROFILE_RELEASE_PANIC=unwind CARGO_HOME=$(CURDIR)/debian/cargo_home make PROFILE=release MULTICALL=$(MULTICALL) \
 				TEST_NO_FAIL_FAST="-- --skip test_dd::test_stdin_stdout_skip_w_multiplier \
 				--skip test_env::test_env_arg_ignore_signal_valid_signals \
 				--skip test_env::test_env_french \
